# Persisted history — API.md §History (persisted series)
#
# Long-term series read back from /data/history, as opposed to /stats which is
# the live rolling 24h. Empty until the writers have produced something: the
# hourly rollups need a completed clock-hour, the daily top-N a completed day.

@base = {{host}}/api/v1
@auth = Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Summary, defaults: last 24h at hour resolution.
GET {{base}}/history/summary
{{auth}}

### Explicit window, one point per UTC day.
GET {{base}}/history/summary?from=2026-07-28T00:00:00Z&resolution=day
{{auth}}

### A 90-day hourly chart: 2160 points, under the 5000 default budget, so
### `stride` comes back as 1 (nothing decimated).
GET {{base}}/history/summary?from=2025-04-25T00:00:00Z&to=2029-07-24T00:00:00Z&resolution=hour
{{auth}}

### A tight budget forces decimation — check `stride` in the response.
GET {{base}}/history/summary?from=2026-08-03T00:00:00Z&to=2029-07-24T00:00:00Z&max_points=5
{{auth}}

### Perf series, defaults: last 24h, budget 1000 (a day is 1440 samples at the
### 60 s cadence, so expect stride 2).
GET {{base}}/history/perf
{{auth}}

### Only what an RSS chart needs — the other keys are ABSENT, not null.
GET {{base}}/history/perf?fields=rss_bytes
{{auth}}

### The compile peak — a `getrusage` high-water mark, so a 360 s sampler records
### it without landing inside the 2.85 s compile. A drop is a restart, never a
### reclaim; 0 means the row predates the field. Far above `rss_bytes` is normal.
GET {{base}}/history/perf?fields=peak_rss
{{auth}}

### Latency + cache only.
GET {{base}}/history/perf?fields=latency,cache
{{auth}}

### Top blocked domains over the last week (both defaults).
GET {{base}}/history/top
{{auth}}

### Top queried domains, 25 of them.
GET {{base}}/history/top?kind=queried&n=25
{{auth}}

### Busiest clients over a month.
GET {{base}}/history/top?kind=clients&from=2026-06-24T00:00:00Z&to=2026-07-29T00:00:00Z
{{auth}}

### A range with no data is 200 with an empty `items` — NOT a 404.
GET {{base}}/history/summary?from=1970-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=1970-01-02T00:00:00Z
{{auth}}

### Bad parameters are REJECTED, not silently ignored — each of these should be
### 400, naming the offending parameter. A backwards window first: `from` is
### after `to`, so the range cannot hold data no matter what is stored.
GET {{base}}/history/summary?from=2029-07-01T00:00:00Z&to=2025-07-24T00:00:00Z
{{auth}}

### `resolution` is hour|day only — `week` is not a silent fallback to `day`.
GET {{base}}/history/summary?resolution=week
{{auth}}

### `kind` is blocked|queried|clients only.
GET {{base}}/history/top?kind=advertisers
{{auth}}

### An unknown `fields` name is rejected rather than ignored, so a typo cannot
### silently remove the series a chart was asking for.
GET {{base}}/history/perf?fields=rss_bytes,rss_byte
{{auth}}

### And a non-numeric budget.
GET {{base}}/history/perf?max_points=lots
{{auth}}
